## 1. JEPA practice papers and their heuristic settings

### LeCun, "A Path Towards Autonomous Machine Intelligence"
v0.9.2, OpenReview BZ5a1r-kVsf, 2022-06-27.

- Non-contrastive JEPA criteria: s_x informative, s_y informative, s_y predictable from s_x, and minimal latent information.
- Criteria 1, 2 and 4 "collectively prevent a collapse".
- Section and figure numbers: [UNVERIFIED].

### I-JEPA: Assran et al., CVPR 2023
arXiv 2301.08243, v1 2023-01-19.

Defaults (App. A.1):

- Predictor: ViT of width 384; depth 6 (ViT-B), 12 (ViT-L/H) or 16 (ViT-G).
- Optimiser: AdamW, batch 2048, lr 1e-4 → 1e-3 (15-epoch warmup) then cosine to 1e-6.
- Weight decay: 0.04 → 0.4 linear.
- EMA: 0.996 → 1.0 linear.
- Masks: 4 target blocks, scale (0.15, 0.2), aspect (0.75, 1.5); 1 context block, scale (0.85, 1.0), with overlap removed. Targets are masked at the target-encoder output.

Ablations (IN-1% linear probe, ViT-B/16, 300 ep unless noted):

| Table | Ablation | Result |
|---|---|---|
| T6 | Masking strategy | multi-block 54.2; rasterized 15.5; block 20.2; random 17.6 |
| T8 | Target scale | (0.075,0.2) 19.2; (0.1,0.2) 39.2; (0.125,0.2) 42.4; **(0.15,0.2) 54.2**; (0.2,0.25) 38.9; (0.2,0.3) 33.6 |
| T9 | Context scale | (0.40,1) 31.2; (0.65,1) 47.1; (0.75,1) 49.3; (0.85,1) 54.2 |
| T10 | Number of target blocks | 1: 9.0; 2: 22.0; 3: 48.5; 4: 54.2 |
| T11 | Target masking location (ViT-H) | output 67.3 vs input 56.1 |
| T12 | Predictor depth (ViT-L, 500 ep) | 6: 64.0; 12: 66.9 |
| T13 | Weight decay (ViT-L, 600 ep) | ramp 0.04→0.4: IN-1% 69.4, linear 77.8; fixed 0.05: 70.7 / 76.4 |
