## 2. Collapse and rank metrics

- **Effective rank** (Roy & Vetterli, EUSIPCO 2007): erank = exp H(p), with p_k = σ_k / ||σ||_1.
- **RankMe** (Garrido et al., ICML 2023; 2210.02885):
  - Same formula with ε added, computed on singular values of the N×K embedding matrix.
  - Uses 25,600 samples, ε ≈ 1e-7.
  - Only for comparisons within one method.
- **LiDAR** (Thilak et al., ICLR 2024; 2312.04000):
  - Smooth rank of Σ_w^{-1/2} Σ_b Σ_w^{-1/2}, with n = 1k samples and q = 50 augmentations.
  - In I-JEPA, RankMe rises early and then falls fast.
  - Kendall τ with probe accuracy: LiDAR 0.86 vs RankMe 0.83.
- **α-ReQ** (Agrawal et al., NeurIPS 2022): power-law exponent of the eigenspectrum.
- **Jing et al. 2022** (2110.09348): log singular values of the centred validation-set covariance, sorted. Some fall to zero under dimensional collapse.
- **SimSiam std**: std of z/||z|| per channel. About 1/√d when healthy, 0 when collapsed.

